Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a function_call with no text still sends content
 (#7307, Yongfei-Hu)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

buildChat left content off an assistant message that called tools and
said nothing: a function_call after a function_call_output, a
function_call with no assistant text before it, or an assistant message
whose text is empty. The message was {"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[…]}
and a strict Chat upstream refused it, 400 "Invalid message at index N:
missing role or content". Codex resends the history, so the session
stayed broken.

The field is content "". A turn that already had text is unchanged.
Parallel calls in one step stay on that message. DeepSeek still gets
reasoning_content. A custom_tool_call is the same turn.

TestResponsesChatFunctionCallAfterOutput failed before the change.
call_after_output message 3, call_with_no_text message 1,
empty_text_then_call message 1, reasoning_then_call message 1,
custom_tool_call_with_no_text message 1, deepseek_call_after_output
message 3 and deepseek_reasoning_then_call message 1 were
{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[…]} (DeepSeek also had
reasoning_content) where the test wanted "content":"" beside the calls.
The shapes that already had text passed on the old code.

Verified under a temporary HOME, with GOPATH, GOMODCACHE and GOCACHE
pinned first:

- go test -count=1 -run TestResponsesChatFunctionCallAfterOutput
  ./internal/gateway: ok.
- go test -race -count=1 -timeout 40m ./internal/gateway/...: FAIL,
  1699.723s. The new test passed. TestUpstreamBodiesUnchanged/responses-to-chat
  failed because testdata/upstream_bodies/responses-to-chat.json still
  omitted content; that file now has "content":"". Re-run of
  TestUpstreamBodiesUnchanged, TestResponsesChatFunctionCallAfterOutput,
  TestChatEmptyAssistant and TestRealtimeHeldToKeyLimit: ok, 2.716s.
- The same package run also failed TestMarshalRawIsEncodingJSON,
  TestMarshalSizedIsJSONMarshal, FuzzMarshalRaw/seed#7,
  TestOpenCodeGoOwnFreeModelGetsNothingOfOpenCodes,
  TestServeWSLListensBesideLoopback and TestServeWSLListensAtVia.
  Those are the failures recorded on origin/main for #7258.
  TestRealtimeHeldToKeyLimit reported a race while another gateway
  suite shared the machine and passed when run alone.
- gofmt -l on the changed Go files: empty.
- go vet ./...: exit 0. Darwin warning, pre-existing:
  internal/proc/disclaim_darwin.go:35 posix_spawn_file_actions_addchdir_np
